%S A402354 2,10,86,1430,44390,2620490,304867686,72193361185,35300294577430,
%T A402354 35676204545593013,74127890831917779662,314487226164961559919173,
%U A402354 2707516294431833177721644490,47078951198111442434893270139516,1647805403208622519504787454786766270
%N A402354 Number of digraphs on n unlabeled nodes, self-loops allowed, that are reducible for every election of source-SCC headers.
%C A402354 An election chooses one node in each source strongly connected component and adds a new root with edges to those chosen nodes. Every such election must yield a reducible flow graph.
%C A402354 Self-loops never affect the election property (transformation T1 deletes them), so in the Burnside computation each conjugacy class gains a factor 2^(number of cycles) for the fixed loop sets. Each qualifying digraph, including its self-loops, is counted once up to isomorphism; the election itself is not distinguished.
%D A402354 F. Harary and E. M. Palmer, Graphical Enumeration, Academic Press, NY, 1973.
%D A402354 M. S. Hecht and J. D. Ullman, Flow graph reducibility, SIAM J. Comput. 1 (1972), 188-202.
%D A402354 M. S. Hecht and J. D. Ullman, Characterizations of reducible flow graphs, J. ACM 21 (1974), 367-375.
%D A402354 R. W. Robinson, Counting digraphs with restrictions on the strong components, in T.-H. Ku (ed.), Combinatorics and Graph Theory '95, World Scientific, Singapore, 1995, pp. 343-354.
%D A402354 R. E. Tarjan, Testing flow graph reducibility, J. Comput. System Sci. 9 (1974), 355-365.
%H A402354 Gregory Morse, <a href="/A402354/b402354.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..23</a>
%H A402354 Gregory Morse, <a href="/A397968/a397968.py.txt">Required Python module (unlabeled_reducible_cfgs.py)</a>, Aug 2026.
%H A402354 Gregory Morse, <a href="/A400123/a400123_1.py.txt">Required Python module (everywhere_reducible.py)</a>, Sep 2026.
%H A402354 Gregory Morse, <a href="/A398465/a398465.py.txt">Required Python module (labeled_reducible_cfgs.py)</a>, Jul 2026.
%H A402354 Gregory Morse, <a href="/A401321/a401321_1.py.txt">Required Python module (valid_header_elections.py)</a>, Oct 2026.
%H A402354 Gregory Morse, <a href="/A399885/a399885.py.txt">Python program (unlabeled_reducible_elections.py)</a>, Nov 2026.
%F A402354 a(n) = (1/n!) * Sum_{sigma in S_n} 2^c(sigma) * F_every(sigma), where c(sigma) is the number of cycles of sigma and F_every(sigma) counts loopless digraphs fixed by sigma for which every election of source-SCC headers is reducible.
%o A402354 (Python)
%o A402354 # Save the five linked Python files in one directory using the filenames
%o A402354 # shown in their link captions, then run Python in that directory.
%o A402354 from unlabeled_reducible_elections import unlabeled_election_sequence
%o A402354 unlabeled_election_sequence("unlabeled_reducible_digraphs_every_loops", 17)
